WEBVTT

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:12.520
This is the fourth in a series of quarterly reports that feature progress being made by NASA's Exploration Launch Projects Office.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:29.970
The Systems Integration Laboratory, or SIL, is the primary facility for the initial integration of the avionics and flight software system.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.350
for the Ares-1 launch vehicle. Located in building 4493 at Marshall Space Flight Center,

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:43.890
the lab gives project engineers their first look at a real-time simulation of the Ares-1

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:51.350
ascent trajectory. The lab configuration and control system, named Maestro, can switch out avionics

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:57.150
packages in order to gather a wide variety of data on the vehicle during flight.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.980
Marshall engineers monitor the

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.240
simulated flight, examining different physical properties of the vehicle during its ascent.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:12.100
Data on pressure, altitude, Mach number, and velocity are gathered to help the vehicle

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.520
designers optimize the configuration of the vehicle's electronics and software systems.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:25.040
At Ames Research Center, another computer simulation has been developed to examine abort scenarios

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:29.960
for the Ares I. Researchers recently completed an examination of positive

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.040
debris impact with the Orion in the event of an ARIES-1 mishap or

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.850
explosion. The results of this study will help vehicle designers in risk

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:46.060
assessment and safety system design. The AIMS team also examined blast wave

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.500
overpressure in the event of an ARIES-1 upper stage explosion to determine what

00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:58.140
effects the blast wave would have on the Orion capsule. A ground wind loads

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.760
checkout model was successfully

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:04.840
tested at Langley Research Center's Transonic Dynamics Tunnel in late March

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:09.940
and early April. These tests address possible failures on the launch pad due

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.240
to ground winds which could cause bending and shearing of the vehicle. This test

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.600
successfully established Langley's capabilities for ground wind load testing.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.270
Lessons learned will be documented and applied to tests currently planned on

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:29.210
the Ares 1-X test configuration and Ares 1 flight configuration.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:35.050
currently scheduled for April 2008 and July 2009, respectively.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:47.180
The Ares 1 five-segment reusable solid rocket booster first stage will be utilizing a newly

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:53.680
reformulated internal motor insulation, thanks to ongoing efforts at Kirkhill Elastomers.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:59.970
Kirkhill Elastomers, based in Brea, California, is a partner with ATK Lawn.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.460
systems. They have been developing and manufacturing the motor internal

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:11.290
insulation of the Space Shuttle Solid Rocket Booster for 25 years. Kirkhill is

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:15.610
in the process of testing a new insulation for the four-segment solid

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:20.750
rocket motor and that insulation will be used on Ares I when full-scale

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:25.860
production of five-segment motors begins. The insulation separates the

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.800
propellant from the steel casing. A new material P

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:35.500
fiber used in protective gear for firefighters is being utilized as part

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:40.460
of Kirkhill's new insulation material. It is first brought together with the

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:45.780
other materials for the insulation in a mixing process. The mixture is then

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:52.310
rolled into sheets and cured on racks. Once cured, the process is repeated and

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:57.320
the sheets are then rolled one last time through a series of rollers in a

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.920
process known as calendaring until

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.700
the desired thickness is achieved. Some of these sheets are then hand rolled and

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:13.980
extruded into the desired shape for use as seals. Kirkhill began reformulating

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.880
its solid rocket motor insulation three years ago in an effort to prevent it

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:23.860
from becoming obsolete. The new insulation is 10% lighter than the

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.460
current insulation, safe for people to handle without personal protective

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.900
of equipment and

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.500
can withstand temperatures of up to 5,000 degrees Fahrenheit

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:35.360
for more than two minutes.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:44.120
Engineers working on the Aries 1 J2X upper stage

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:48.430
and Aries 5 RS 68 core stage engines

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:51.010
recently completed a series of tests

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.130
on subscale injector hardware.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.380
This test series focused on modifications

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.210
to the injector tips to improve performance.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:05.380
The series also sought to determine the optimal number of injector elements per square inch

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:11.120
to provide the best balance of performance versus manufacturability and cost.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:19.770
Between February and April of 2007, Marshall engineers conducted 14 hot fire tests

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:24.170
on 28, 40, and 58 element injectors.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:29.980
These injectors channel liquid hydrogen and liquid oxygen into the engine's main...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:37.160
combustion chamber. Firings of roughly 7 to 20 seconds generated between 15,000

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:42.730
and 20,000 pounds of thrust over a range of chamber operating temperatures and

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:47.640
pressures. These tests found that higher element density led to better

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:53.240
performance. For the J2X engine, which is focusing on injectors of between 40

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:58.820
and 58 elements, this verifies their projected performance expectations as

00:05:58.910 --> 00:05:59.970
as well as verifying the

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.460
stability of the J2X at these element densities.

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:09.540
Heat flux data obtained from the test firings will also aid in the design of the engine's

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.980
main combustion chamber.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:23.490
In another nod to the legacy of launch vehicles inherited by Ares, work is underway at Marshall's

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:29.890
Building 4755 to prepare for the arrival of a friction stir welding tool from

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.680
MTS systems of Eden Prairie, Minnesota. This facility was previously used in

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:41.530
assembly of the Saturn 1C and the friction stir welding process itself is

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:48.040
utilized on the Space Shuttle external tank. A robotic weld tool very similar to

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.340
the new system being installed at Marshall was in use on Space Shuttle tank

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:58.170
hardware but was damaged by Hurricane Katrina. Excavation and installation of

00:06:58.170 --> 00:06:59.970
reinforcing material has been

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:05.420
completed and rods that will be used in mounting the tool have been placed. A

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:10.380
representative from MTS has also inspected the facilities work to ensure

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:15.680
smooth installation of the tool upon its arrival. The friction stir welding

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.700
process will be used to assemble different components of the upper stage

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:24.760
in the same manner as has been developed under the external tank program for the

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.500
space shuttle. The robotic welding tool will be shipped to Marshall and assembled

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:29.960
on Sunday.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.520
as the finish machine is too complex and too massive to transport fully assembled.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:43.630
The friction stir welding process uses a very rapidly spinning pin to fuse two pieces of metal together.

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:50.160
This creates a bond significantly stronger and less prone to breakage than traditional welding,

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:55.760
with fewer defects in the finished product, even under microscopic examination.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.730
The upper stage office has also recently

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:05.030
begun confidence panel testing for the upper stage instrument unit. These panels

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:10.250
will test the manufacturing and rolling ability of aluminum lithium panels with

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.550
different rib thicknesses as part of weight reduction efforts on the upper

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:21.150
stage. First sheets of aluminum lithium are hand examined via ultrasound to check

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:26.140
for internal defects in the raw material. Once the material has been hand

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:29.890
inspected, the surface is skimmed to ensure it is

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.700
as flat as possible, and a cutting tool then cuts a grid pattern into the material.

00:08:36.210 --> 00:08:40.510
The thickness of the resultant ribs is then verified by hand.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.920
For the confidence panels, a variety of different rib thicknesses are examined to determine

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:50.380
the ideal thickness of the final instrument unit panels.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:57.010
After the panels are cut, a fluorescent penetrant liquid is painted over the entire surface.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.920
This liquid will seep into any crack.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.600
cracks or other defects in the finished panel and can then be drawn out by application of

00:09:05.600 --> 00:09:11.590
a second developer chemical. The panel is then inspected under black light to illuminate

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:17.110
any spots on the panel where the penetrant has found its way into cracks or porosity

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:27.980
defects. In April, engineers at White Sands Test Facility conducted tests of the Peacekeeper

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.520
missile's axial engine

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.630
potential use as a roll control system on the Ares 1-X test flight. This engine

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:43.020
produces approximately 2,500 pounds of thrust. Subsequent tests at the end of

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:49.660
April provided Ares 1-X with valuable data on the Peacekeeper engine. Analysis

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:54.520
of the data is underway now to determine the suitability of this engine for use

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:59.870
as a roll control solution on the test flight. For more information about Ares

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:06.800
plans and progress, visit us on the web at nasa.gov slash ARIES.
